{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>נאור [illuminated]</b> — No thing appears to be honorable that is not a body and an actual substance, except light alone." "And the word נאור — like נכון [established]. And this corresponds to 'כבוד' [honor] and 'אדיר' [mighty], as in: 'אדיר במרום ה׳ [Mighty on high is YHWH].'" "<b>מהררי טרף [from mountains of prey]</b> — that no person can ascend there. R. Moses the Kohen said: if the enemy who is frightened by Him seeks refuge in the mountains, from where wild beasts come down, he will not escape. And there is no sense in his words. Also the commentators said: for נאור is from the root of נאר מקדשו [stricken from His sanctuary], like משחית [destroying], and the nun is a root letter. And indeed it is an adjective like קרוב [near] and רחוק [far], except that it is a transitive verb, like: ושבח אני [and I praise]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 76, :notes {2 "Resolved 'הצר שנפחד ממנו' as 'the enemy who is frightened by Him'; the referent of the fear is ambiguous in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:42.839270036Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}